}, {\"distinct_partners\": 9, \"events\": 12, \"node\": 881}, {\"distinct_partners\": 12, \"events\": 18, \"node\": 991}, {\"distinct_partners\": 11, \"events\": 17, \"node\": 1034}, {\"distinct_partners\": 6, \"events\": 9, \"node\": 1641}], \"window\": [65552, 70552]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 32925, "tokens_after": 32925, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"rows_scanned": 102480, "step_id": "step_10", "tool": "window_event_count", "args": {"windows": [[56322, 63322], [63322, 68322], [68322, 70552], [70552, 73322], [73322, 80322], [80322, 86322]], "nodes": [58, 247, 277, 383, 424, 429, 721, 794, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1291]}, "result_digest": "4f4cfc047e0aff1f", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 217, \"window\": [56322, 63322]}, {\"n_events\": 131, \"window\": [63322, 68322]}, {\"n_events\": 58, \"window\": [68322, 70552]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [70552, 73322]}, {\"n_events\": 12, \"window\": [73322, 80322]}, {\"n_events\": 3, \"window\": [80322, 86322]}]}", "latency_ms": 8, "tokens_before": 43163, "tokens_after": 43163, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"rows_scanned": 102480, "step_id": "step_11", "tool": "window_event_count", "args": {"windows": [[56322, 63322], [63322, 68322], [68322, 70552], [70552, 73322], [73322, 80322], [80322, 86322]], "nodes": [138, 393, 402, 613, 686, 861, 879, 895, 928, 944, 970, 1014, 1032, 1605]}, "result_digest": "67070e36fbe82700", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [56322, 63322]}, {\"n_events\": 4, \"window\": [63322, 68322]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [68322, 70552]}, {\"n_events\": 35, \"window\": [70552, 73322]}, {\"n_events\": 267, \"window\": [73322, 80322]}, {\"n_events\": 225, \"window\": [80322, 86322]}]}", "latency_ms": 5, "tokens_before": 43163, "tokens_after": 43163, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"rows_scanned": 17080, "step_id": "step_12", "tool": "burst_detection", "args": {"nodes": [59, 83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 743, 826, 881, 991, 1034, 1641], "window": [56322, 86322], "n_bins": 12, "z_threshold": 1.5}, "result_digest": "1a48ab04eba26cb1", "result_summary": "{\"bursts\": [], \"mean\": 92.08, \"n_bursts\": 0, \"sd\": 17.44, \"z_threshold\": 1.5}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 54161, "tokens_after": 54161, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_107b45e5", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "regime_switch", "entities": [59, 83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 743, 826, 881, 991, 1034, 1641], "window": [56322, 86322], "confidence": 0.9, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Neighborhood evolution with a 5000-unit half-window gives peak dissimilarity 1.00 at t=70552, versus a stable ~0.28-0.42 baseline elsewhere, exceeding the 0.6 criterion. Snapshot diff across the change point shows zero overlap (Jaccard 0.0, 120 edges removed / 86 added), and the old contact cohort's traffic falls 217->131->58->1 while the new cohort's rises 1->35->267 in the same instant, confirming a sharp substitution rather than gradual drift. Confounds were controlled: no activity burst (z>=1.5) and near-flat group volume rule out a volume artifact; and because the entire graph rewires in this window (global Jaccard 0.0012), a matched control of equally active nodes was profiled and showed saturated ~0.97 turnover at every probe with no localized peak, so the group's low-baseline-plus-single-spike signature is specific to it and not explained by popularity or global churn."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: an abrupt regime switch is present.**\n\nKey evidence:\n- **Peak dissimilarity = 1.0** at t\u224870552 (step_01), far above the 0.6 threshold. Baseline turnover elsewhere in the window sits at ~0.28\u20130.42, so the spike is a genuine discontinuity, not the background rate.\n- **Complete partner substitution**: the group's edge sets before/after 70552 share nothing (Jaccard 0.0; 120 edges removed, 86 added \u2014 step_04). Old cohort {58, 247, 277, 383, 424, 429, 721, 794, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1291} collapses from 217\u2192131\u219258\u2192**1** event (step_10) exactly as the new cohort {138, 393, 402, 613, 686, 861, 879, 895, 928, 944, 970, 1014, 1032, 1605} rises 1\u219235\u2192267 (step_11). The handoff is essentially instantaneous.\n- **Confounders ruled out**: (a) *Not volume-driven* \u2014 no activity burst at any z\u22651.5 (step_12); group volume is roughly flat (192/172/110/207, step_03) and actually dips slightly at the change point. (b) *Not popularity/global churn* \u2014 the whole graph rewires (global Jaccard 0.0012, step_05), so a matched control of comparably active nodes (882, 1551, 1947, 1784) was tested: its turnover is pinned at ~0.95\u20131.0 across *every* probe with no distinguishable peak (step_08). Our group is different precisely because it has a low, stable baseline punctuated by one spike. (c) *Not a static artifact* \u2014 degrees are ordinary and stable through the pre-window (step_09).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_107b45e5\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [59, 83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 743, 826, 881, 991, 1034, 1641],\n  \"window\": [56322, 86322],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Neighborhood evolution with a 5000-unit half-window gives peak dissimilarity 1.00 at t=70552, versus a stable ~0.28-0.42 baseline elsewhere, exceeding the 0.6 criterion. Snapshot diff across the change point shows zero overlap (Jaccard 0.0, 120 edges removed / 86 added), and the old contact cohort's traffic falls 217->131->58->1 while the new cohort's rises 1->35->267 in the same instant, confirming a sharp substitution rather than gradual drift. Confounds were controlled: no activity burst (z>=1.5) and near-flat group volume rule out a volume artifact; and because the entire graph rewires in this window (global Jaccard 0.0012), a matched control of equally active nodes was profiled and showed saturated ~0.97 turnover at every probe with no localized peak, so the group's low-baseline-plus-single-spike signature is specific to it and not explained by popularity or global churn.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 65384, "total_output_tokens": 4505, "total_tokens": 69889, "total_latency_ms": 69452, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}